// Dev/perf-test script, not sample content — delete this file (or the trigger block below) once
// you're done stress-testing. It has no gameplay purpose.
//
// Spawns 100 stationary NPCs around whichever player joins the world, each wearing 'player_model'
// and looping a different animation clip, so you can watch F3's frame time with a real crowd of
// skinned+animated entities instead of guessing from code. Behaviour is fixed at STATIONARY (no
// pathfinding/look-at) so this measures render+animation cost specifically, not AI-goal-tick cost —
// see NpcStressTestCommands' own doc for why those are kept separate.
//
// `once` means this fires the first time each player joins this world after the script loads, not
// every single login — remove the trigger (or the whole file) when you're done, otherwise it stays
// armed for the next `/reload` or world load.
//
// Want a bigger/smaller crowd? Change the '100' below, or skip the trigger entirely and just run
// `/sme npc stresstest 100` (or any count up to 500) whenever you like — same underlying spawn.

story npc_stress_test {

    trigger on_join_stress_test {
        when event player.join
        once
        run {
            npc_spawn_stress_test 100
        }
    }
}
